course: dictionary
lesson: 7287
title: What is pinyin?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Pinyin is a way of writing Chinese sounds with the letters we use in English. «Pinyin writes Chinese sounds with Latin letters and tone marks; it helps learners with pronunciation.» If you can read pinyin, you can have a go at saying Chinese words.
explain: Chinese is written with thousands of characters, not an alphabet, so learners often start with pinyin. «It is written with thousands of characters instead of an alphabet, so learners use pinyin to help them along.» Pinyin is a helper for reading and speaking before you learn the characters.
explain: Pinyin also uses tone marks. «We write what you hear in pinyin, with little tone marks showing whether the voice stays high, rises, dips or falls.» The marks sit over the vowels, as in mā, má, mǎ and mà, and they show how your voice should move on each one.
fact: Pinyin is the official way of writing Chinese (Mandarin) words with the Latin letters we use for English.
fact: Pinyin shows the tones of Mandarin with little marks over the vowels, such as mā, má, mǎ and mà.
fact: Children in China learn pinyin at school, and it is used for typing Chinese on phones.
fact: Place names like Beijing are written in pinyin.
fact: A word in pinyin, such as «ni hao», is Chinese, not English.
exercise: «Pinyin writes Chinese sounds with Latin letters.» What does pinyin do? | *It writes Chinese sounds with the letters we use in English | It is a kind of Chinese food | It translates English into French | Draws Chinese characters with a brush
exercise: Which of these shows a tone mark over a vowel? | Beijing | hello | *mà | the
exercise: «Place names like Beijing are written in pinyin.» Which of these is a place name written in pinyin? | Tuesday | Hello | *Beijing | Tone
test: Where do children in China learn pinyin? | On television only | At home, with no lessons at all | *At school | Only at university
test: What do the little marks over vowels show? | The size of the letters | Which word is English | The name of the writer | *Whether the voice stays high, rises, dips or falls
exam: Why is pinyin useful for a learner who has not yet learned Chinese characters? | It stops them needing to learn any sounds | It replaces the need to speak at all | Pinyin is only used on English websites | *It lets them read and say Mandarin words using Latin letters
